.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fB\%<Xm/ExtP\&.h>\fP declares the helpers that the widgets of the Motif
extension library (ColorSelector, FontSelector, Tree, Outline, TabBox,
ComboBox2 and others) share\&.  They are exported for these widgets and
their subclasses, and are not meant for applications\&.
.PP
\fB\%_XmConfigureWidget\fP, \fB\%_XmMoveWidget\fP and
\fB\%_XmResizeWidget\fP call
\fB\%XtConfigureWidget\fP, \fB\%XtMoveWidget\fP and
\fB\%XtResizeWidget\fP between
\fB\%XmDropSiteStartUpdate\fP and \fB\%XmDropSiteEndUpdate\fP, so that
the drop
sites follow; \fB\%_XmConfigureWidget\fP makes a width or height of 0
into 1\&.
.PP
\fB\%_XmRequestNewSize\fP asks the parent of \fIw\fP for the size
\fIwidth\fP by
\fIheight\fP (only asks, if \fIquery_only\fP), accepts a compromise, and
returns in \fIr_width\fP and \fIr_height\fP the size that is or would be
allowed\&.  \fB\%_XmHWQuery\fP is the end of a query_geometry method
that
cares only about width and height: \fIpreferred\fP holds the preferred
size, and the result is \fB\%XtGeometryYes\fP if \fIintended\fP gives
exactly
that size, \fB\%XtGeometryNo\fP if it gives another size or, when
\fIintended\fP is NULL, if the preferred size is the current one, and
\fB\%XtGeometryAlmost\fP otherwise\&.
.PP
\fB\%_XmSetValuesOnChildren\fP calls \fB\%XtSetValues\fP with \fIargs\fP
on every
descendant of \fIw\fP\&.  \fB\%_XmFilterArgs\fP copies \fIargs\fP
without the
resources named in the NULL-terminated list \fIfilter\fP, into a new
list
that the caller frees with \fB\%XtFree\fP\&.  \fB\%_XmGetFocus\fP is an
action
procedure that gives the focus to \fIw\fP (\fB\%XmProcessTraversal\fP
with
\fB\%XmTRAVERSE_CURRENT\fP)\&.  \fB\%_XmGetMBStringFromXmString\fP
returns the text
of an XmString, with a newline for each separator, in a new string
that the caller frees with \fB\%XtFree\fP, or NULL\&.
\fB\%_XmGadgetWarning\fP prints a warning and returns True if \fIw\fP is
a
gadget, for widgets that do not support gadget children\&.
\fB\%_XmUtilIsSubclassByNameQ\fP tells whether the class of \fIw\fP, or
one of
its superclasses, is named by the quark \fInameq\fP\&.
\fB\%_XmExtHighlightBorder\fP and \fB\%_XmExtUnhighlightBorder\fP call
the
border highlight or unhighlight method of Primitive or Gadget on
\fIw\fP\&.
.PP
\fB\%XmResolveAllPartOffsets64\fP is \fB\%XmResolveAllPartOffsets\fP for
classes whose parts must be aligned on 8 bytes: on a system where
pointers are larger than int (all 64-bit systems), all parts are
aligned on 8 bytes; otherwise the part of the class is\&.
.SH "BUGS"
.PP
\fB\%_XmGetMBStringFromXmString\fP frees \fIxmstr\fP with
\fB\%XmStringFree\fP
when it holds no component it can read\&.
